 "query": "I stopped at the corner community garden on my walk over this morning, and the whole bed of sunflowers right by the fence is finally fully open, their heads so heavy with seeds they\u2019re tilting almost all the way over the path. A tiny calico kitten was curled up napping on the lowest wooden slat of the raised bed, and it let me scratch behind its ears for a full five minutes before it stretched, yawned so wide its little pink tongue curled, and trotted off after a bumblebee bumbling between the zinnia rows. One of the regular gardeners was passing out handfuls of the super sweet cherry tomatoes they\u2019d grown, sun-warmed and so juicy they dripped down my wrist when I bit into one, and they said the vines are producing so much right now anyone can take as many as they want for the rest of the week. I\u2019ve been seeing synthetic hair extensions and little wig storage pouches priced under 30 floating around my feed lately. I\u2019ve heard so much buzz about that cool dark two-tone color, the one that\u2019s like black mixed with that other shade people keep raving about lately, yeah that one. All of those bits line up exactly with the stuff that\u2019s been on my radar as I scroll.",
